WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.566
In this Cloud Minute, I want to show you

00:00:01.566 --> 00:00:04.566
how to deploy Microsoft SQL Server on a Google Compute

00:00:04.566 --> 00:00:07.566
Engine instance. In Google Cloud Developer Console

00:00:07.566 --> 00:00:10.566
Go to Compute Engine and create an instance

00:00:10.566 --> 00:00:13.566
Give it a name, select its zone

00:00:13.566 --> 00:00:16.566
and then machine type

00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:19.566
For boot disk, choose one of the SQL Server images provided

00:00:19.566 --> 00:00:22.566
And hit create

00:00:22.566 --> 00:00:25.566
Once the instance is ready

00:00:25.566 --> 00:00:28.566
You can create a Windows user and password and remote desktop

00:00:28.566 --> 00:00:31.566
into it like any other Windows instance

00:00:34.566 --> 00:00:37.566
Once logged in

00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:40.566
You can use SQL Server Management Studio

00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:43.066
to connect and manage the SQL Server instance

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
You can check out the links in the description

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
of the video for more information

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:53.900
Thanks for watching!

